{{also|bursten|Bürsten}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|bürsten}}; see {{m|de|Borste|t=brush, bristle}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈbʏʁstən/}}
* {{rhymes|de|ʏʁstən|s=2}}
* {{audio|de|De-bürsten.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[scrub]], to clean a surface with a [[brush]] {{q|but not usually teeth, for which {{m|de|putzen}}}}
#: {{ux|de|Die Kacheln müsste ich mal richtig '''bürsten'''.|I have to properly '''brush''' these tiles sometime.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[brush]] {{q|hair, fur}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''bürste''' dir kurz die Haare.|I’ll '''brush''' your hair quickly.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[brush]] someone’s [[hair]] or the [[fur]] of an animal {{q|should be used with caution regarding other people because of the vulgar sense below}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''bürste''' meinen  Hund mehrmals pro Woche.|I '''brush''' my dog several times a week.}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[brush]] one’s own hair
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''bürste''' mich kurz.|I’ll '''brush''' my '''hair''' quickly.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|uncommon|vulgar}} to [[fuck]], to [[have sex]] with

====Usage notes====
* {{m|de|kämmen|Kämmen|lit=to comb}} is often preferred with hair, even when the device used is a brush rather than a comb.

